# Line endings are part of this repository's contract.
#
# manifest.json records the SHA256 of every generated artifact, and
# engine/scripts/verify_manifest.py / build.py --verify-only compare raw bytes.
# Without an explicit eol, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces
# CRLF working-tree files whose hashes never match, so the maintainer cannot run
# the repository's own provenance gates locally; conversely a CRLF commit would
# fail verify_manifest in CI while the text-based gates (parity_check, the
# golden-byte job) still pass, pointing diagnosis in the wrong direction.
#
# Pin LF for every text file: the builders already write newline="\n".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending convert binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mmdb binary
